  "changes": [
    "Repeated startup, including the installer auto-launch, opens common settings in the existing instance instead of the Tartarus board.",
    "The unified application uses its own Torchlight Overlay profile instead of sharing the old Tartarus Overlay singleton/profile.",
    "One-time preferences/Local Storage/IndexedDB import keeps the original profile read-only, refuses active/unknown database copies and preserves existing new-profile data.",
    "The single-instance lock is acquired before any migration/settings write; early repeated launches are queued until settings can be shown."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Electron remains the Tartarus UI host. This release does not implement a fully native UI; Board is retained for explicit correction.",
    "Close the old app before the first 1.0.1 launch to import its stored confirmations/cache. Active database copies are skipped rather than overwritten.",
    "Tests use isolated profiles and do not install over or stop the user's running application."
  ],
